    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e6170e9_b9678bf9",
        "filename": "src/crosvm/sys/unix.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1389,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-23T22:37:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a lot of code that assumes `#[cfg(unix)]` implies KVM, but I think it would be a worthwhile cleanup to put KVM hypervisor support behind `--features\u003dkvm` and fix those implicit assumptions.\n\nNobody is working on this right now, as far as I\u0027m aware, but it should be easier  once we have a second hypervisor implementation to validate everything still compiles with kvm disabled.",
